<title>GREECE: Greek May C/A deficit rises 23.3pct y/y to $801mln.</title>
<headline>Greek May C/A deficit rises 23.3pct y/y to $801mln.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's current account deficit rose a provisional 23.3 percent to $801 million in May from $649.8 million in the same month a year ago, the Bank of Greece said in a statement.  </p>
<p>The January-May deficit widened to $2.697 billion from $1.988 billion in the same period in 1995, it said.</p>
<p>The trade deficit rose to $7.573 billion in the first five months of 1996 from $7.156 in the same period in 1995.</p>
</text>
